 "intro": "Near Mount Gindarus in northern Syria, 38 BC. The Parthian prince Pacorus has invaded Syria again. You are Publius Ventidius Bassus, Mark Antony’s general, who as a boy was paraded as a captive in a Roman triumph.",
 "debrief": "In Cassius Dio’s and Frontinus’s accounts, Ventidius tricked a spy into telling Pacorus to take a longer route, which gave him time to gather his legions. Camped on high ground, he let the Parthians charge uphill, then counter-attacked with legionaries and slingers. Pacorus was killed and the Parthians fled. The battle was said to fall on the anniversary of Carrhae. Ventidius became the first Roman to celebrate a triumph over Parthia. The other choices are what-ifs.",
